                  "x"
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Each rule is a quotient of a square root function and a polynomial, continuous on its domain. At the join, the left rule approaches 3 / 5 and f(1) = 3(4) / 20 = 3 / 5, so f is continuous at x = 1 and on [-8, -4) U (-4, 5) U (5, 17].",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               3,
               [
                  "Sqrt",
                  16
               ]
            ],
            20
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The piece that contains x = 0 is (-4, 5), open at both ends. Its integers are -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3 and 4.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            -3,
            -2,
            -1,
            0,
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The sum of those integers is 4.",
         "mathjson": 4
      }
